  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering leaders and families to conserve and protect ecosystem services of the Montecillos Biological Reserve and improve food security</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communities in and near the Montecillos Biological Reserve face challenges of living and farming in and adjacent to protected areas with increasing environmental limitations on water and soil resources. Centro de Enseanza Aprendizaje de Agricultura Sostenible El Socorro (CEASO) encourages families to use the Finca Humana (Human Farm) approach to establish a more reliable food supply and provides technical assistance in ecosystem restoration and agroforestry and sustainable farming. At the IAF, we support community-led solutions to expand economic opportunity in Honduras. CEASO&apos;s activities promote smallholder agriculture and food production to enhance food security and ensure meaningful opportunities for communities to thrive. This grant is part of the IAF&apos;s efforts to address the root causes of irregular migration in Central America.</narrative>
  </description>
